    "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/bb19cd7175e3e2ad8108d2405e8159d0.avif?t=1739520798\" width=608 height=149 /></span><br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel set aboard the BUB - a living forest adrift in space. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about something ancient and evil adrift in space. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about hell. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about judgment. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about a girl who summons a forest spirit. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a magical stag that lives in the woods in space.<br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about a girl who is losing her mind. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about a talking cat. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about love and madness. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about time and space. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a visual novel about the corporatization of justice. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is trying to avoid being too political. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is built by history. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is built by philosophy. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is about getting endings and achievements. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is about going outside and making friends. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is about doing what it takes to survive. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a tale you\u2019ve heard before. <br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is something entirely new.<br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a horror game.<br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a coven-building sim set in space.<br><strong>Satan is an Astronaut</strong> is a friend-killing sim set in the imagination of a mentally disturbed young woman.<br>                 <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/973311bd4d1b2d5e3b00a1224bd2e3b7.webp?t=1739520798\" width=143 height=19 /></span> is a person who goes to space<br>                 <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/3cbe87c79e3f2b800fa7eebeee09cf9a.webp?t=1739520798\" width=184 height=26 /></span> is someone who understands space. <br>                          <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/b519ac5c261a43886d3b54d662ac15cc.webp?t=1739520798\" width=160 height=50 /></span> is the accuser and the adversary.<br>                          <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/c44572dbda46cd6bd85601a3da398336.webp?t=1739520798\" width=197 height=63 /></span> is the beginning and the end.<br>                                 <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/5316339951ebfd5f91e2b14e8fe8a971.avif?t=1739520798\" width=505 height=74 /></span><br><br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3062530/extras/32f341aedb44184eab4d65b927375175.avif?t=1739520798\" width=608 height=150 /></span><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Enjoy truly <strong>spectacular original art</strong> and gameplay from Matt de Carvalho.<br></li><li>Experience <strong>original music and fearsome sound design</strong> from Shane Stephenson. <br></li><li>Explore a fine <strong>story about cats and devils and space</strong> and what can happen when people really buy into your madness without fully thinking it through, written by Ryan Moriarty.<br></li><li><strong>Hours of fun!</strong> (About two, if I\u2019m honest, but that warrants a plural by DEFINITION.)<br></li><li><strong>Multiple endings</strong> - some of them make a lot of sense and will speak to you, others, you\u2019ll wonder what I was thinking about when I wrote them. I have a degree in English Lit, so allow me to pre-handwave with a \u201cWhat do you think it means?\u201d <br></li><li><strong>Branching paths where you CHOOSE</strong> who gets to live and who gets to die. Don\u2019t let that power go to your head in real life, though! We don\u2019t need any more lawsuits.</li></ul>",
